<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39218" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prōvīsus</span></b> ,
			ūs (only in <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>abl. sing.</i>), m.
			provideo (Tacitean). * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A looking before</i>, <i>looking into
				the distance</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne oculi quidem provisu juvabant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					3, 22</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b> * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A foreseeing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">periculi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					1, 27</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A caring for</i> or <i>furnishing
				beforehand</i>, <i>precaution</i>, <i>providing</i>, <i>providence</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deūm,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					12, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dispositu provisuque civilium rerum peritus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. H.
					2, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rei frumentariae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. A.
					15, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">curā, provisu deinde agere ac si
					hostis ingrueret,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 12, 12</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
